<item>
            <title>[LU-20579] sanity-lnet test_109 needs ifconfig, absent on minimal images</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20579</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_109 in lustre/tests/sanity-lnet.sh creates and removes an interface alias with ifconfig:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;	ifconfig &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$FAKE_IF_ALIAS&quot;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$FAKE_IP_ALIAS&quot;&lt;/span&gt; up ||
		error &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;Failed to add fake IF alias&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
...
	ifconfig &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$FAKE_IF_ALIAS&quot;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$FAKE_IP_ALIAS&quot;&lt;/span&gt; down ||
		error &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;Failed to clean up fake IF alias&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ifconfig comes from net-tools, which is deprecated and is not installed on minimal RHEL 9 / Rocky 9 images. On such a node the test fails at setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are the only two ifconfig calls in the suite. setup_fakeif(), which runs immediately before them in the same test, already uses ip(8) throughout, so the dependency is inconsistent as well as unnecessary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The equivalent ip(8) commands produce the same aliased address:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;# ip addr add 10.1.2.31/31 dev test1pg label test1pg:0
# ip -o -4 a s test1pg
5: test1pg    inet 10.1.2.3/31 scope global test1pg
5: test1pg    inet 10.1.2.31/31 scope global test1pg:0
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suggested fix: use ip addr add ... label and ip addr del, matching the rest of the suite.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
